## Epistemic Invariant — how data tiers work in this system

Every value in the fleet carries its epistemic status. The four tiers:

| Tier | Label | Meaning |
|---|----|---|
| 1 | INTUITED | Vibe with footnotes — raw LLM output, gut, narrative |
| 2 | STRUCTURED | Honest heuristic — reproducible rule, judgement weights |
| 3 | MEASURED | Empirically calibrated — data + CI + sample size + drift monitor |
| 4 | PROVEN | Mathematically proven — closed form + verified preconditions |

**The min-rule:** A value's status is the minimum of its own claim, its inputs' statuses, and its preconditions. Status can never be laundered upward. A stale value (past `valid_until`) auto-demotes one tier.

**P0 incident:** Any layer that claims a higher status than its inputs can support is a laundering condition. Gap ≥ 2 tiers = BLACK signal = system halt. This is not a warning — it is a stop.

**Promotion gates:** INTUITED → STRUCTURED requires rubric codification. STRUCTURED → MEASURED requires ≥10 events per parameter per outcome class + CI + drift monitor. MEASURED → PROVEN requires formal proof + verified preconditions. Skipping tiers is forbidden.

**Attribution:** Every value carries provenance. Name your sources. Claim what is yours. Standing on shoulders of amoeba.

Reference implementation: `~/clean-build/02_build/epistemic_core/epistemic_invariant.py`

